he uses that name, the three times Bitcoin showed up before it clicked, and why sound money and sound craft share a backbone.\nBitcoin crossed his path three times. First in a London bar around 2010. Then in 2018, while he was teaching himself about money. Then in 2024, when, as he puts it, it actually started doing what people said it would do.\nHis first Lightning payment was at a small Italian family restaurant in South London. \"My thoughts became zaps and those zaps became food in your belly.\"\nHe also tells the 16-hour, mud-soaked Glastonbury story that taught him to work smart instead of long, talks about AI as one more tool from someone who lived through the second wave of 3D printing, and offers this to the next generation of makers: \"I'd quite like to be around for a while, so I'll take things slow.\"\nYour 2 sats go to Bitcoin For The Arts and help fund artists. This episode is also free on YouTube: https://youtu.be/ZepNitUDItg\nIN THIS EPISODE:\nWhy he calls himself a general handychap. Work at the Saatchi Gallery, Glastonbury, the Wall Street Journal Apple Car, and a K-2SO build. Discovering Bitcoin three times before it clicked. The first Lightning payment, and zaps that became dinner. The Glastonbury lesson in low time preference. AI as another tool, from a maker who has seen tool waves before. Advice for working makers: take it slow.\nABOUT BITCOIN FOR THE ARTS:\n501(c)(3) nonprofit empowering artists with Bitcoin grants, education, and sovereign funding tools.\nhttps://www.bitcoinforthearts.org\nGrants https://www.bitcoinforthearts.org/grants/apply\nDonate https://www.bitcoinforthearts.org/donate\nYouTube https://www.youtube.com/@BitcoinForTheArts\n⚡Zap 21 sats to unlock this note on\nhttps://fanfares.io/naddr/naddr1qvzqqqr6dgpzpg88x557qj6fwzsct6ryhz086ms769y0muyrsx65ptqzpf6zcck4qyvhwumn8ghj7enpdenxzun9wvhxummnw3erztnrdaksqfpexc6kgdf4xsuj6dmyvvmj6dp5x56z6wpe89jz6cesvs6nqwp5v5cnsce3v45wxe","created_at":1792015226,"id":"abc2e307ce1343d98f756288c1eb9